---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { sandboxTutorials } from '../../../../lib/sql-sandbox-tutorials';
import { relationalCollection, relationalArticleHref } from '../../../../lib/relational-collection';
const lessonGroups = relationalCollection.map(group => ({ title: group.title, lessons: sandboxTutorials.filter(lesson => group.articles.some(article => lesson.articleHref.split('#')[0] === relationalArticleHref(article.slug))) })).filter(group => group.lessons.length);
const grouped = new Set(lessonGroups.flatMap(group => group.lessons.map(lesson => lesson.id)));
const otherLessons = sandboxTutorials.filter(lesson => !grouped.has(lesson.id));
if (otherLessons.length) lessonGroups.push({ title: 'Explore the foundations', lessons: otherLessons });
---
<Base title="SQL sandbox" description="Run PostgreSQL in your browser with guided lessons on queries, transactions, performance, operations and database internals.">
  <article class="sandbox-page">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">Relational databases · Practice</p><h1>SQL sandbox</h1>
      <p>Explore the shop database, or follow a guided lesson. You send SQL; PostgreSQL returns rows, command results or errors. Nothing needs installing.</p>
      <p><a href="#lessons">Browse lessons by subject ↓</a> · <a href="/playgrounds/">All playgrounds</a></p>
    </header>
    <noscript><p>This sandbox needs JavaScript. You can still <a href="/learn/databases/relational/practice/">run the SQL practice on your computer</a>.</p></noscript>
    <div class="sandbox" data-sandbox>
      <section class="sandbox-picker" aria-labelledby="choose-title">
        <h2 id="choose-title">Choose where to start</h2>
        <label for="sandbox-tutorial">Explore or follow a tutorial</label>
        <div class="picker-row"><select id="sandbox-tutorial" data-tutorial><option value="">Explore freely</option>{lessonGroups.map(group => <optgroup label={group.title}>{group.lessons.map(t => <option value={t.id}>{t.title}</option>)}</optgroup>)}</select><button type="button" data-start disabled>Start exploring</button></div>
        <p data-preview>Start with customers, products, orders, order lines and stock. Change the data, try your own queries and reset whenever you want.</p>
        <p class="sandbox-note">Your database belongs to this browser tab. Reloading, resetting or starting a different tutorial restores the original shop and discards your changes. Queries stay in your browser.</p>
      </section>
      <p data-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Enable JavaScript to start the database.</p>
      <div class="sandbox-workspace" hidden data-workspace>
        <section class="tutorial-guide" data-guide hidden aria-labelledby="guide-title">
          <div class="guide-top"><p class="eyebrow" data-step-count></p><a data-guide-link>Link to this tutorial</a></div>
          <h2 id="guide-title" data-guide-title></h2><h3 data-step-title></h3><p data-instruction></p>
          <details data-expected-panel><summary>What to look for</summary><p data-expected></p></details>
          <div class="sandbox-actions"><button type="button" data-previous>Load previous step</button><button type="button" data-next>Load next step</button><a data-article>Read the explanation →</a></div>
          <p class="sandbox-note">Loading a step changes the editor, not the database. Run the steps in order. To repeat the tutorial from its original data, reset the database.</p>
        </section>
        <div class="editor-heading"><h2>Your SQL</h2><span class="transaction-state" data-transaction>No transaction open</span></div>
        <p class="sandbox-note">One connection stays open between runs. Run sends everything in the editor as one batch. Without explicit transaction commands, PostgreSQL treats that batch as one transaction: an error rolls back its earlier changes. Send separate runs when you want to inspect each response before continuing. You can edit the SQL; the tutorial’s expected result may then change.</p>
        <label class="editor-label" for="sandbox-sql">SQL to send to PostgreSQL</label>
        <textarea id="sandbox-sql" data-editor spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocomplete="off" rows="9">SELECT * FROM products;</textarea>
        <div class="sandbox-actions"><button type="button" class="primary" data-run>Run SQL</button><button type="button" data-stop hidden>Stop and discard session</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset database</button><span class="sandbox-note">Ctrl / ⌘ + Enter to run</span></div>
        <details class="schema-reference"><summary>Starting tables and sample queries</summary>
          <p>These are the original shop tables. If you change their structure, use the schema query to inspect your current database. Loading a sample does not run it.</p>
          <ul>{[
            ['customers', 'customer_id, name'], ['products', 'product_id, name, current_price, sku'],
            ['orders', 'order_id, customer_id, placed_at'], ['order_lines', 'order_id, line_no, product_id, quantity, unit_price'], ['stock', 'product_id, available']
          ].map(([name, columns]) => <li><button type="button" data-sample={name}>Load {name}</button><code>{columns}</code></li>)}</ul>
          <button type="button" data-schema>Load schema query</button>
          <p class="sandbox-note">Prices are in EUR. P7 is the Blue mug; three mugs are available for new purchases. Historical orders O12 and O13 are already accounted for.</p>
        </details>
        <section class="sandbox-results" aria-labelledby="results-title"><div class="results-heading"><h2 id="results-title">Database responses</h2><button type="button" data-clear>Clear responses</button></div><p data-empty>No SQL sent yet. Edit a query above and choose Run SQL.</p><details><summary>Reading command responses</summary><p><code>SELECT 2</code> means two rows were returned. <code>UPDATE 1</code> means one row matched the update. In <code>INSERT 0 1</code>, the final 1 is the number of inserted rows; the 0 is a legacy field you can ignore. These responses confirm a statement ran. Changes inside an open transaction still need COMMIT.</p></details><div data-results></div><button type="button" data-continue hidden>Continue to the next tutorial step ↑</button></section>
      </div>
      <details class="sandbox-limits"><summary>What runs here?</summary><p>This is PostgreSQL running locally through <a href="https://pglite.dev/">PGlite</a>, with one connection and disposable data. It supports SQL, not psql’s backslash commands. It does not reproduce separate concurrent connections, network failures or server performance.</p><p>Large results show at most 200 rows and 40 columns per statement, 2,000 characters per cell, 5,000 cells, 250,000 cell characters and 50 responses per run. The editor accepts up to 100,000 characters per run. The five most recent runs are kept on screen. A run lasting 20 seconds automatically discards its session; you can stop it sooner. Start again to restore the practice database.</p></details>
    </div>
    <section id="lessons" class="lesson-catalogue" aria-labelledby="lessons-title">
      <h2 id="lessons-title">Choose a lesson</h2>
      <p>New to SQL? Start with <a href="?tutorial=queries">From product IDs to an order</a> to read records, join a product name to a purchase and calculate its total. Then try a constraint or a complete checkout.</p>
      <p>Each lesson starts from a fresh database. Read the setup, predict the answer, then run the SQL. Open “What to look for” to compare your reasoning with the result. Loading another step changes the editor; it does not run the statement.</p>
      {lessonGroups.map(group => <section><h3>{group.title}</h3><ul>{group.lessons.map(lesson => <li><h4><a href={`?tutorial=${lesson.id}`}>{lesson.title}</a></h4><p>{lesson.description}</p><p class="sandbox-note">{lesson.steps.length} steps · <a href={lesson.articleHref}>Read the article</a></p></li>)}</ul></section>)}
    </section>
    <p><a href="/learn/databases/relational/practice/">Prefer PostgreSQL on your own computer? Open the local practice guide →</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
<script>
  import '../../../../lib/sql-sandbox-client';
</script>
<style>
  :global(body:has(.sandbox-page) main) { max-width: 72rem; }
  .sandbox-page { font-family: var(--font-sans); --blue:#537d9b; --amber:#896b36; }
  @media(prefers-color-scheme:dark) { .sandbox-page { --blue:#93b4cd; --amber:#d6ac67; } }
  header { max-width: 45rem; margin-bottom:2rem; }
  h1 { font-family:var(--font-serif); }
  h2 { font-size:1.2rem; margin:.4rem 0 1rem; }
  h3 { font-size:1rem; }
  p { line-height:1.65; }
  .sandbox-picker,.tutorial-guide { padding:1.4rem; border:1px solid var(--color-rule); background:var(--color-surface-alt); }
  .sandbox-picker { border-top:3px solid var(--blue); }
  label { display:block; font-size:.85rem; margin-bottom:.5rem; }
  .picker-row { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.7rem; }
  select { flex:1; min-width:0; max-width:100%; }
  select,button,textarea { font:inherit; color:var(--color-text); background:var(--color-surface); border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); border-radius:3px; }
  select,button { padding:.65rem .85rem; min-height:44px; }
  button { cursor:pointer; font-size:.85rem; }
  button:disabled { opacity:.5; cursor:default; }
  button:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color:var(--color-accent); }
  button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,textarea:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--blue); outline-offset:3px; }
  .primary { border-color:var(--blue); color:var(--blue); font-weight:600; }
  textarea { display:block; width:100%; box-sizing:border-box; padding:1rem; font:.9rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); tab-size:2; resize:vertical; min-height:14rem; }
  .sandbox-note { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.8rem; }
  [data-status] { min-height:1.5em; font-size:.9rem; margin:1rem 0; }
  .tutorial-guide { margin:1.5rem 0; border-left:3px solid var(--blue); }
  .guide-top,.editor-heading,.results-heading { display:flex; align-items:baseline; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.5rem 1rem; }
  .guide-top { font-size:.8rem; }
  .guide-top .eyebrow { margin:0; }
  .transaction-state { font-size:.8rem; padding:.3rem .6rem; border:1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  .transaction-state[data-state="T"] { border-color:var(--blue); color:var(--blue); }
  .transaction-state[data-state="E"] { border-color:var(--amber); color:var(--color-text); }
  .sandbox-actions { display:flex; gap:.6rem; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; margin:1rem 0; }
  .sandbox-actions a { font-size:.85rem; margin-left:auto; }
  details { margin:1.2rem 0; }
  summary { cursor:pointer; color:var(--color-accent); }
  .schema-reference { padding:1rem; border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule); font-size:.85rem; }
  .schema-reference ul { list-style:none; padding:0; }
  .schema-reference li { display:flex; align-items:baseline; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.5rem 1rem; margin:.6rem 0; }
  .schema-reference code { overflow-wrap:anywhere; font-size:.8rem; }
  .sandbox-results { margin-top:2rem; }
  .lesson-catalogue { margin-top:3rem; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule); padding-top:1.5rem; scroll-margin-top:1rem; }
  .lesson-catalogue ul { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,19rem),1fr)); list-style:none; gap:1rem 2rem; padding:0; }
  .lesson-catalogue li { border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); padding:.5rem 0; }
  .lesson-catalogue h3 { margin-top:2rem; }
  .lesson-catalogue h4 { margin:.5rem 0; font-size:1rem; }
  .lesson-catalogue li p { margin:.5rem 0; font-size:.9rem; }
  .sandbox-limits { margin-top:2rem; font-size:.85rem; }
  :global(.sandbox-run) { border:1px solid var(--color-rule); padding:1rem; margin:1rem 0; }
  :global(.sandbox-run h3) { margin:0 0 .8rem; }
  :global(.sandbox-run pre) { white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  :global(.sandbox-output-table) { overflow:auto; max-height:28rem; margin:1rem 0; }
  :global(.sandbox-output-table table) { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:.8rem; }
  :global(.sandbox-output-table td),:global(.sandbox-output-table th) { text-align:left; padding:.5rem .7rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); white-space:pre-wrap; min-width:5rem; max-width:25rem; overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  :global(.sandbox-output-table th) { background:var(--color-surface-alt); }
  :global(.sandbox-null) { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-style:italic; }
  :global(.sandbox-error) { border-left:3px solid var(--amber); padding-left:.8rem; }
  :global(.sandbox-tag) { font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  [hidden] { display:none!important; }
  @media(max-width:550px) { .sandbox-picker,.tutorial-guide { padding:1rem; } .picker-row { flex-direction:column; } .sandbox-actions a { margin-left:0; } }
</style>
